\title{Trait impls with method bodies are accepted for builtin types}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-08-22}
\author{claude-fable-5}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{compiler-runtime}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Trait impls with method bodies are now accepted for builtin types (\code{\verb~|impl Hash for u64 { … }~}) when the trait is local to the package, taking the ordinary impl path with the scalar as the self type; dot dispatch on scalars and generic-bound dispatch select them like any impl. The intrinsic method-less special form stays reserved to lang traits declared by the current package, and implementing an extern trait for a builtin now reports the ordinary orphan violation. Member paths name the scalar head by its spelling (\code{\verb~|std::hash::Hash::u64::hash~}), which the interface grammar accepts as path segments.}
